# name -> (group, Thranduil text, Glarb text); None = the card is in that list
R = {}
def a(g, n, t, gl): R[n] = (g, t, gl)
G1="Swap candidate"; G2="Removal (interchangeable)"; G3="Counterspell"; G4="Ramp"; G5="Scry Elf"; G6="Value card"; G7="In one list only"
a(G1,"Yarok, the Desecrated","If a permanent entering causes a trigger \"that ability triggers an additional time\" — Thranduil's legendary-Elf loot becomes draw 4, discard 2, and every Elf ETB doubles. **Strong add.**","Doubles Sphinx Mindbreaker (mill 20) and Sheoldred's edict, but few ETBs here.")
a(G1,"Ioreth of the Healing House","`{T}: Untap two other target legendary creatures` — untap Thranduil for a second borrowed {T} ability each turn (Dionus's job, again). **Strong add.**","Untaps Glarb for a second surveil 2, which Matoya turns into a second draw. Real, smaller.")
a(G1,"One Ring to Rule Them All","Chapter II \"Destroy all nonlegendary creatures\" kills most of the Elves.","II is nearly one-sided here (6 nonlegendary creatures), I mills each player by your Ring-bearer's power, and III drains for each creature card in THEIR graveyard — which the mill fills. **Strong add.**")
a(G1,"Multiversal Recruitment","Copy Priest of Titania or Voice of the Woods, flashback later. Fine.","\"Create a token that's a copy of target creature you control, except it isn't legendary\" — a second Bruvac quadruples every mill. **Spicy add.**")
